%% claude-code-lane-lock — drift block sequence
%% The hero mechanism: UserPromptSubmit exits 2, harness erases the prompt
%% from context before any reasoning token fires.
%%
%% Render: https://mermaid.live, or drop inside a ```mermaid fence on GitHub.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant CC as Claude Code harness
    participant UPS as UserPromptSubmit hook<br/>(bin/user-prompt-submit.mjs)
    participant Match as lib/match.mjs
    participant Pin as lib/pin.mjs
    participant Lock as ~/.claude/lane-lock/<br/>sessions/&lt;session_id&gt;.json

    Note over User,Lock: Session is pinned to ~/projects/project-alpha/

    User->>CC: types "work on project-beta"
    CC->>UPS: spawn hook, pipe {prompt, session_id, cwd} to stdin
    UPS->>Pin: loadPin(session_id)
    Pin->>Lock: read lockfile
    Lock-->>Pin: { project_root: .../project-alpha, aliases: [project-alpha] }
    Pin-->>UPS: pin = project-alpha
    UPS->>Match: scanPrompt(prompt, siblingAliases)
    Note right of Match: regex matches "project-beta"<br/>as sibling alias token
    Match-->>UPS: { decision: "block", reason: "alias", token: "project-beta" }
    UPS->>CC: stderr: "lane-lock: drift prompt BLOCKED before reasoning started<br/>(sibling 'project-beta' detected, pin=project-alpha)"
    UPS->>CC: exit 2

    rect rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.15)
      Note over CC: harness sees exit 2 on UserPromptSubmit<br/>→ ERASES the prompt from context<br/>→ 0 reasoning tokens spent
    end

    CC-->>User: prompt erased, session still pinned to project-alpha

    Note over User,Lock: To cross lanes on purpose, prefix the prompt:<br/>"[cross-lane: project-beta] glance at the pattern"<br/>match.mjs sees the escape hatch → allow + warn
